        "title": "Definition & Function",
        "content": "    Thaana (𐴦) serves as a vowel elongation diacritic within the Rohingya script. Its primary phonological function is to extend the duration of the vowel sound associated with the preceding consonant, effectively doubling its length. For instance, the character 𐴁 represents the sound /b/ with a short vowel; when the Thaana is appended as in 𐴁𐴦, the syllable's nucleus is lengthened, producing /baː/ (a long 'aa' sound)."
